This equation is satisfied when:

(1)  $x^{2} + 16x + 60 = 0  \Rightarrow  (x + 6)(x + 10) = 0  \Rightarrow  x = -6, -10$ ;

(2)  $x^{2} - 9x + 19 = 1  \Rightarrow  x^{2} - 9x + 18 = 0  \Rightarrow  (x - 3)(x - 6) = 0  \Rightarrow  x = 3, 6$ ;

(3)  $x^{2} - 9x + 19 = -1  \Rightarrow  x^{2} - 9x + 20 = 0  \Rightarrow  (x - 4)(x - 5) = 0  \Rightarrow  x = 4, 5$ of which  $x = 5$  is eliminated from (3) since the exponent  $5^{2} + 16(5) + 60 = 165$  is odd and  $(-1)^{165} = -1$  (a contradiction).  Hence, the solution set is  $x = \{-10, -6, 3, 4\} \cup \{6\}$ , or  $\fbox{5}$  values.

